      "question": "Given y = (5x^2 - 10x + 9)/(x - 1)^2, x not equal to 1, show that dy/dx = k/(x - 1)^3 where k is a constant to be found.",
      "status": "ready",
      "answer": "k = -8, so dy/dx = -8/(x - 1)^3",
      "steps": [
        "Write y = u/v with u = 5x^2 - 10x + 9 and v = (x - 1)^2.",
        "Quotient rule: dy/dx = (v du/dx - u dv/dx)/v^2.",
        "du/dx = 10x - 10 = 10(x - 1) and dv/dx = 2(x - 1).",
        "Numerator = 10(x - 1)(x - 1)^2 - 2(x - 1)(5x^2 - 10x + 9).",
        "Factor 2(x - 1): numerator = 2(x - 1)[5(x - 1)^2 - (5x^2 - 10x + 9)].",
        "Bracket = 5x^2 - 10x + 5 - 5x^2 + 10x - 9 = -4, so numerator = -8(x - 1).",
        "Divide by v^2 = (x - 1)^4: dy/dx = -8(x - 1)/(x - 1)^4 = -8/(x - 1)^3.",
        "So k = -8."
      ],
      "images": [
